---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Join Us">
  <main class="wrap feature-index join-compact">
    <div class="feature-index-intro"><span>JOIN US / SYSAL</span><h1>Join Us</h1><p>We welcome enquiries from prospective researchers whose interests align with our work.</p></div>
    <section class="join-compact-list" aria-label="Ways to work with SysAL">
      <article class="join-compact-row"><span>01</span><div><h2>PhD researchers</h2><p>We welcome enquiries from prospective PhD students interested in our research areas. Opportunities depend on research fit, supervisory capacity and funding.</p></div></article>
      <article class="join-compact-row"><span>02</span><div><h2>Postdoctoral researchers</h2><p>We welcome conversations about postdoctoral research and fellowship applications, including externally funded opportunities. Any position or hosting arrangement depends on funding, eligibility and research alignment.</p></div></article>
      <article class="join-compact-row"><span>03</span><div><h2>Undergraduate and postgraduate researchers</h2><p>We work with undergraduate MEng, MSc and MRes researchers through research projects and programmes such as UROP and IROP, subject to availability and a good match with ongoing work.</p></div></article>
      <article class="join-compact-row"><span>04</span><div><h2>Visitors</h2><p>We welcome enquiries about focused research visits from students and researchers at other institutions, where there is a clear collaborative project and practical arrangements can be agreed.</p></div></article>
    </section>
    <section class="join-compact-contact" aria-label="Contact"><h2>Get in touch</h2><p>Interested in joining SysAL? Please get in touch with <a href="https://profiles.imperial.ac.uk/david.boyle">David Boyle</a>, Associate Professor at Imperial College London, with a brief description of your background, research interests and the opportunity you have in mind.</p></section>
  </main>
</Base>
